<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mieszko I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 930–992</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Mieszko I of Poland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mieszko I was the first historically documented ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast dynasty</a>, ruling from around 960 until 992. He married the Bohemian princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doubravka-of-bohemia">Dobrawa</a> and was baptised in 966, an event seen as the beginning of Polish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. He expanded his realm to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> and Silesia, and around 991 placed it under papal protection in the document known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagome-iudex">Dagome iudex</a>.</p></div>
